            <div xml:id="d125">

                <pb facs="0195" n="127" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg127"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72111 Em 1/32½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        President Wilson
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 10, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I am in receipt of your
                    letter of yesterday in regard to the reply to the Austro-Hungarian statement. I
                    approve very heartily of the change which you made as to the paragraph to be
                    inserted on page 9. I will have our reply prepared and sent as soon as possible,
                    and also arrange for its publication here, as I think it will have a salutary
                    effect upon public opinion which is undoubtedly being seriously affected by the
                    propaganda against the exportation of arms and ammunition.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
